 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Precision:** Exponential operations $\exp(-\delta_i \sigma_i)$ can underflow if $\delta_i \sigma_i$ is large. Use standard floating-point arithmetic; if $\sigma_i$ is very large, $T_{i+1}$ becomes 0, which is correct physically [S1, unofficial].
-- **Boundary Conditions:** The derivative is only defined for $i < N$ because $\sigma_N$ does not exist (only $c_N$). The background color $c_N$ is typically not optimized [S1, unofficial].
-- **SH Colors:** When optimizing SH coefficients, the gradient must be multiplied by the SH basis function value at the query direction. The basis values are constant for a given ray direction [S1, unofficial].
