 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ for computing transmittance, weights, and gradients. The density gradient calculation involves a nested loop in the naive implementation shown, but can be optimized to $O(N)$ by precomputing suffix sums of $c_k w_k$. The provided pseudocode is $O(N^2)$ due to the inner sum; an implementer should optimize this [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ to store $T$, $w$, and intermediate sums.
-- **Strengths:** Provides exact gradients, enabling stable and efficient optimization of PlenOctree densities and colors. Avoids numerical instability associated with finite differences [S1, unofficial].
-- **Limitations:** Requires explicit storage of segment properties. Not directly applicable to differentiable volume rendering methods that do not use piecewise constant density [S1, unofficial].
